  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ray parallel to principal axis is incident at $30^{\\circ}$ from normal on concave mirror having radius of curvature $R$. The point on principal axis where rays are focussed is $Q$ such that $\\mathrm{PQ}$ is\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/rueiuBD3_u-ZkcDC2Wdf5GeygQBjLNAolOzYsaqtes0.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XXOpP",
      "text": "$\\frac{R}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rkXkw",
      "text": "$\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hICkX",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\sqrt{R}-R}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DwxGM",
      "text": "$R\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From similar triangles,\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/XHNSXpn6kBt78iTdzYBxZhp-Uyp1yRN1TqalGBhb0xg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\frac{Q C}{\\sin 30^{\\circ}}=\\frac{R}{\\sin 120^{\\circ}}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nor $\\quad Q C=R \\times \\frac{\\sin 30^{\\circ}}{\\sin 120^{\\circ}}=\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{3}}$\r\n\r\nThus $P Q=P C-Q C=R-\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{3}}=R\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
